arch=arm64
vmlinux_btf=6.12 kernel BTF dump (bpftool btf dump file <BTF copied from /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux> format c, Amazon Linux 2023 aarch64, 6.12.113-138.209.amzn2023.aarch64)
clang=Ubuntu clang version 18.1.3 (1ubuntu1)
load_verified=none
notes=rebuilt because bpf/rt_file.bpf.c changed: each program checks the cgroup
  allowlist before resolving the event's path. Same 8 program sections and 14
  programs as the object it replaces; same header as the previous build. Its
  struct renamedata still has new_dir and no new_parent, so compiling against
  it keeps exercising the bpf_core_field_exists() fallback path that the x86
  object's 7.0 header cannot reach. CO-RE resolves field offsets against the
  kernel the object is loaded on, not the header.
